the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    the calculation date is *a date*; scenario element.
    *a person* is a dependent of *a tax unit*; scenario element.
    the ctc child amount under subsection h is *an amount*.
    the ctc joint phase out threshold under subsection h is *an amount*.
    the ctc other phase out threshold under subsection h is *an amount*.
    the ctc other dependent amount under subsection h is *an amount*.
    the ctc refundable per child cap under subsection h is *an amount*.
    the ctc refundable phase in threshold under subsection h is *an amount*.
    *a person* is ctc child ssn requirement satisfied under subsection h.
    *a person* is ctc child credit disallowed by ssn requirement under subsection h.
    *a person* is ctc qualifying child under subsection h.
    *a person* is ctc other dependent under subsection h.
    the ctc qualifying children under subsection h of *a tax unit* is *a number*.
    the ctc other dependents under subsection h of *a tax unit* is *a number*.
    the ctc phase out threshold under subsection h of *a tax unit* is *an amount*.
    the ctc maximum before phase out under subsection h of *a tax unit* is *an amount*.
    the ctc refundable maximum under subsection h of *a tax unit* is *an amount*.
    *a person* is taxpayer or spouse ssn included on return; scenario element.
    *a person* is qualifying child ssn included on return; scenario element.
    the taxpayer or spouse ssn of *a person* is valid for subsection h; scenario element.
    the qualifying child ssn of *a person* is valid for subsection h; scenario element.
    the ctc child of *a person* satisfies subsection c; scenario element.
    the ctc person of *a person* satisfies dependency rules; scenario element.
    *a person* is noncitizen exception to other dependent credit under subsection h; scenario element.
    the filing status of *a tax unit* is *a code*; scenario element.

the knowledge base us_statutes_26_24_h includes:


% 26 U.S.C. 24(h) — us:statutes/26/24/h
the text of "26 USC 24(h)(2)" is at "sources/us/statutes/26/24/h.yaml".

the text of "26 USC 24(h)(3)" is at "sources/us/statutes/26/24/h.yaml".

the text of "26 USC 24(h)(4)(A)" is at "sources/us/statutes/26/24/h.yaml".

the text of "26 USC 24(h)(5)" is at "sources/us/statutes/26/24/h.yaml".

the text of "26 USC 24(h)(6)" is at "sources/us/statutes/26/24/h.yaml".

the text of "26 USC 24(h)(7)" is at "sources/us/statutes/26/24/h.yaml".

the text of "26 USC 24(h)(4)" is at "sources/us/statutes/26/24/h.yaml".

the text of "26 USC 24(h)(2), 24(h)(7)" is at "sources/us/statutes/26/24/h.yaml".

the text of "26 USC 24(h)(2), 24(h)(4)" is at "sources/us/statutes/26/24/h.yaml".

the ctc child amount under subsection h is 2200 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2018-01-01 <= D.

the ctc joint phase out threshold under subsection h is 400000 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2018-01-01 <= D.

the ctc other phase out threshold under subsection h is 200000 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2018-01-01 <= D.

the ctc other dependent amount under subsection h is 500 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2018-01-01 <= D.

the ctc refundable per child cap under subsection h is 1400 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2018-01-01 <= D.

the ctc refundable phase in threshold under subsection h is 2500 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2018-01-01 <= D.

rule ctc_child_ssn_requirement_satisfied_under_subsection_h with provenance "26 USC 24(h)(7)":
a person is ctc child ssn requirement satisfied under subsection h if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2018-01-01 <= D
    and the person is taxpayer or spouse ssn included on return
        and the person is qualifying child ssn included on return
        and the taxpayer or spouse ssn of the person is valid for subsection h
        and the qualifying child ssn of the person is valid for subsection h.

rule ctc_child_credit_disallowed_by_ssn_requirement_under_subsection_h with provenance "26 USC 24(h)(7)":
a person is ctc child credit disallowed by ssn requirement under subsection h if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2018-01-01 <= D
    and the ctc child of the person satisfies subsection c
        and it is not the case that the person is ctc child ssn requirement satisfied under subsection h.

rule ctc_qualifying_child_under_subsection_h with provenance "26 USC 24(h)(7)":
a person is ctc qualifying child under subsection h if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2018-01-01 <= D
    and the ctc child of the person satisfies subsection c
        and the person is ctc child ssn requirement satisfied under subsection h.

rule ctc_other_dependent_under_subsection_h_1 with provenance "26 USC 24(h)(4)":
a person is ctc other dependent under subsection h if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2018-01-01 <= D
    and the ctc person of the person satisfies dependency rules
        and it is not the case that the ctc child of the person satisfies subsection c
        and it is not the case that the person is noncitizen exception to other dependent credit under subsection h.

rule ctc_other_dependent_under_subsection_h_2 with provenance "26 USC 24(h)(4)":
a person is ctc other dependent under subsection h if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2018-01-01 <= D
    and the person is ctc child credit disallowed by ssn requirement under subsection h.

rule ctc_qualifying_children_under_subsection_h with provenance "26 USC 24(h)(2), 24(h)(7)":
the ctc qualifying children under subsection h of a tax unit is a number N if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2018-01-01 <= D
    and the tax unit is a tax_unit
        and N is the count of each P such that
            a person P is a dependent of the tax unit
            and P is ctc qualifying child under subsection h.

rule ctc_other_dependents_under_subsection_h with provenance "26 USC 24(h)(4)":
the ctc other dependents under subsection h of a tax unit is a number N if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2018-01-01 <= D
    and the tax unit is a tax_unit
        and N is the count of each P such that
            a person P is a dependent of the tax unit
            and P is ctc other dependent under subsection h.

rule ctc_phase_out_threshold_under_subsection_h with provenance "26 USC 24(h)(3)":
the ctc phase out threshold under subsection h of a tax unit is an amount if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2018-01-01 <= D
    and the filing status of the tax unit is a code C
        and C = 1
        and the ctc joint phase out threshold under subsection h is the amount
        otherwise the tax unit is a tax_unit
        and the ctc other phase out threshold under subsection h is the amount.

rule ctc_maximum_before_phase_out_under_subsection_h with provenance "26 USC 24(h)(2), 24(h)(4)":
the ctc maximum before phase out under subsection h of a tax unit is an amount N if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2018-01-01 <= D
    and the ctc qualifying children under subsection h of the tax unit is a number M
        and the ctc child amount under subsection h is an amount K
        and the ctc other dependents under subsection h of the tax unit is a number P
        and the ctc other dependent amount under subsection h is an amount Q
        and N = M * K + P * Q.

rule ctc_refundable_maximum_under_subsection_h with provenance "26 USC 24(h)(5)":
the ctc refundable maximum under subsection h of a tax unit is an amount N if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2018-01-01 <= D
    and the ctc qualifying children under subsection h of the tax unit is a number M
        and the ctc refundable per child cap under subsection h is an amount K
        and N = M * K.

